I'm trying to get some of these TVs in  the building turned off because you got  too many people talking on TV about us  and what they think about us what we  should do what we are what we're not but  they don't really know who we are or  what we're capable of people or what  we're going through what we're thinking  it's just the outside viewers looking in  and so yeah tunnel vision ear muffs and  just come to work every day and try to  get better and get back to what we know  we're capable of doing that's been true  for Biscay talking to reporters on  wednesday once the TV's turned off in  Hallas hall and look I think I know what  he was trying to do and it was kind of I  don't want to say tongue-in-cheek but  look it always bugs me when football  players or coaches get mad because those  of us who are paid to observe and  comment on what we see observe a bad  team and comment on how badly the team  is performing how dare we acknowledge  the obvious Chris so look I don't think  it it requires a PhD in high level  fandom to understand that the Bears  stink right now I don't know where Mitch  true Biscay wants people to say they're  great they're just misunderstood right  they're getting screwed by the refs no  they stink yeah no there's no doubt  about it and you know he you know he  himself is going in the wrong direction  this year the other offense has been  horrible  you know the defense is still really  good but they haven't been as dominant  because the offense is so bad this year  they're out there every fourth play of  the game so they wear down eventually so  it's yeah it's not a good look and you  know I understand like them not wanting  like turn the TV's off do that thing or  change the channel yeah there's a lot of  teams that do that especially when  they're struggling I mean I've been a  part of that I can remember a year in  Tampa where we were struggling and Jon  Gruden was walking out of the cafeteria  and turned the TV off because he just  didn't want to hear it like I think the  NFL Network was on at that time or  whatever it may be now I know other  organizations who don't have TVs in  their building to begin with anyways  where the players are you know lounging  around it's it's not about that you're  here to work we're not here to like sit  together and watch TV and and gossip and  talk about what's going on in the world  New England you know I don't know how  they've done with their  new facility I know they've redone stuff  up there but when I worked there there  was no TVs around guys weren't gonna be  sitting there listening to outside noise  and having conversations about oh this  guy said this and this guy said that so  it is something that is dealt with in  the building in different ways  throughout the NFL and and I'd like to  try to articulate a basic rule of thumb  that I had never really thought about  before yeah I think if a team is being  criticized undeservedly they use that  noise as motivation yes when a team is  being criticized for good reasons that's  when you just don't want to hear it  because they're right right I mean you  can use this bulletin board material  when you think that somebody's being  unfair in their criticism of a player a  coach a team whatever but when they are  dead-on accurate that's when you just  turn it off because you know it's  forcing you to look in the mirror and  you know it's not a pretty sight that's  exactly right you know a lot of you like  the Eagles two years ago with the Super  Bowl run right I mean they had the  confidence and knew at that point that  they were a really good team when Carson  Wentz got hurt so they weren't about to  go like oh we got to turn the TV off  teams are you know the people on TV are  telling us we have no chance of winning  with Nick Foles they were like no screw  that let's listen to these idiots talk  we're really awesome we're not just  about one player and they did rally  around that and the flipside yes usually  when teams are 2 and 5 or whatever it  may be 2 and 6 and just playing crappy  all together there's no defense of it  because usually that's the truth of the  matter you know players haven't played  well the coaches have messed up in  certain situations their schemes haven't  been good whatever it may be and yeah  that's when it doesn't become motivation  at all it becomes let's not listen to  the outside noise let's not start  fighting each other because of the  outside noise and see if we can rally  together just by let's get better here  in the building and practice and get on  our P's and Q's and cross our T's and  dot our eyes and all that crap now with  all that said yeah and the Bears turn it  around do you see anything there that  gives you hope that what Mitchell true  Biscay is saying is accurate and that  they know the team better than the rest  of us and that they are going to find a  way I mean you know it feels like there  Owen 8 they are through  five yeah did win three in a row and  they had a Lions team coming to town  that has found a way more often than not  to lose games that maybe they should  have won this year well I feel like it  doesn't really matter who they play  every games gonna be close cuz their  offense isn't capable of blowing anybody  out of the water so and I don't really  have the confidence that their offense  is gonna come through really at this  point in late-game situations to win  football games and what's scary too is  even when they do come through let's  just say and get a lead you know we've  seen here this year where the defense is  too exhausted at that time to hold the  lead down anyways you know whether it be  the Raiders game in London that's the  one that jumps out to me more than  anything but you know I look at their  schedule and just go man okay they're  you know the Lions the Giants the Lions  again you know those are teams that I  could say yeah make it beat them but  they could very easily lose because  their offense is capable of laying an  egg there's still no identity and then  when you talk about Chiefs Vikings Green  Bay Dallas Cowboys and Rams I go know  those teams are better than the Chicago  Bears and it's going to take a defensive  pick six or a fumble or a short field or  things like that for them to win those  type of games in my opinion yeah and  here's the problem the NFC has so many  great teams is sheer right they're gonna  have to run the table or come damn close  to so Bears want to get back to the  playoffs seven and one yeah I think  minimum nine and seven is probably not  going to get you in in the NFC this year  and they've got the Vikings and the  Packers on their own division they got  the Packers again this year they they  got to go to Lambeau Field and play  Green Bay they've got to go to Minnesota  and play the Vikings it would be and  every year there's a team hovering  around 500 that finds the gas pedal in  November and takes off it would be a  stunner if the Bears are the ones who do  it because we've seen the bodywork so  far yeah not good yeah  hi I'm Mike Tirico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from NBC  Sports

